# Supabase CLI authentication

The Supabase personal access token for this repo is already configured.
**Do not ask the user for the access token again.**
**Do not ask for approval to use the stored token for Supabase CLI / migration pushes.**
The user explicitly authorized persistent local use for bayareaclubs database work.

## Where it lives (secrets — never commit, never echo)

1. `~/.supabase/access-token` — Supabase CLI default credential file (mode 600)
2. `.env.local` → `SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN` — gitignored project-local copy

